%% OpenHub -- Team claim lifecycle (v5.1)
%% Statuses and transitions of a claim of the team-state, as allowed by
%% teamstate.ValidTransitions, with where the lease and the end of a session
%% (teamstate.DecideClaimEnd) act. A claim is a file of the team-state:
%% "released" means the file is removed.
%% The lease is not a status: "expired" is a property of a claim worked on
%% (Claim.IsExpired), judged by oh doctor, oh team claim and, when
%% release_expired_on_sync is set, the tracker synchronization.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> planned : tracker plan
    [*] --> in_progress : oh team claim, session start

    planned --> in_progress : work starts

    in_progress --> review : review published, team board, MCP verdict
    in_progress --> blocked : blocked

    blocked --> in_progress : unblocked

    review --> validation : moved on the board
    review --> done : approved, merged
    review --> in_progress : sent back

    validation --> done : accepted
    validation --> review : back to review
    validation --> in_progress : sent back

    done --> in_progress : reopen
    done --> [*] : removed after done_retention_days

    planned --> [*] : released
    in_progress --> [*] : released
    blocked --> [*] : released
    review --> [*] : released by its owner only

    note right of planned
        No lease: nobody renews a planned claim,
        a claim of the initial column or a pool claim
    end note

    note right of in_progress
        Lease lease_until, from lease_hours when a session works on it
        The daemon renews it while the session is open
        Renewal stops for a session asleep for sleeping_renewal_days
        or a remote session launched remote_renewal_days ago
        Claim taken by hand, no session: lease_hours_manual, not renewed
        oh team claim on your own claim renews it
        Past the lease the claim is expired and another member can take it over
    end note

    note right of review
        Status review, or label review or ready-for-review on the ticket
        in Beads: the claim never expires and stays reserved
        until the merge or until its owner releases it
        oh doctor only reports it after stale_days
    end note

    note left of done
        End of a session, first rule that applies:
        claim already finished: kept
        ticket closed: claim moves to its terminal status
        in review: kept
        checkpoint waiting, commit checkpoint put off with work left,
        or state unreadable: kept with the label session-ended
        otherwise: released
    end note
